					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-12 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/214/455656700_21397c4161.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" /><br />My man Cesar C (left) repped Massline all Saturday in Bellingham during the annual NW Filipino American Student Alliance Conference with that nifty shirt (yeah i said nifty).<br /><br /><img src="http://farm1.static.flickr.com/250/455633475_b40d2628c2.jpg?v=0" alt="" width="430" /><br />The first Arts and Culture workshop group got a special treat as Geo (top right) was able to sit in and bust the first verse from &quot;Kick Bush&quot; while explaining his method of madness for the song. Later that night, Blue Scholars rocked an event for ColorsNW.<br /><br />Blue Scholars stay busy with a show this week in Salem Oregon for &quot;Conscious Overdose 2007&quot;, alongside labelmates Common Market.  It&#39;s then off to the east coast where the Scholars will make their trek to Bethlehem (in PA, not that far east) and Columbia University in New York City.<br /><br />Big shout out to Don Anus, I mean - Imus as he is going through his best week ever, as VH1 would say. Heh. Somebody really needs to call him out on <em>his</em> hair, forrealdoe.<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-10 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><span class="body1 style18"><span style="line-height: 14px" class="Apple-style-span"><div>Blue Scholars Limited Artist Edition T-shirt designed by <strong><span style="line-height: 14px" class="Apple-style-span">OneSevenNine </span></strong><span style="line-height: 14px" class="Apple-style-span">have been printed and are ready for pre-order (shipping 4/25). These saucy shirts are available for $30 - and is printed on premium quality gray tees. T-Shirts will also be available at shows beginning May 2007. Show some love and get it get it right here: </span><br /></div><div><span style="color: #0000ee; text-decoration: underline" class="Apple-style-span">www.bluescholars.com/artistedition</span></div></span></span><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-09 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>Teaching artists should not be sent to jail for asking about the well-being of their students. The madness has to stop. Come through tomorrow!!!<br /><br /><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">TUESDAY, APRIL 10TH @ 2:30PM</span><div><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">AT KING COUNTY CORRECTIONAL FACILITY</span></div><div><span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">500 5TH AVE, SEATTLE, WA<br /></span><br /><strong>Rajnii</strong>&#39;s personal account is below... if you know my music, you know Rajnii. If you know Rajnii, you know there aren&#39;t that many people more committed to justice, truth-telling and raising up the next generation than him.  <br /><br />ON APRIL 5TH APPROX 3:30PM ON RAINIER AND HENDERSON OUT SIDE RAINIER BEACH HIGHSCHOOL I WITNESSED A HUGE GROUP OF POLICE JUST OUTSIDE THE GATE OF LAKE WASHINGTON APTS.<br /> <br />AS I WALKED TOWARD THE SCHOOL I SAW ONE OF THE CAST MEMBERS IN THE PLAY I&#39;M DIRECTING, TIA HOLIDAY AND SHE TOLD  ME HER CLASSMATE WAS BEING ARRESTED FOR SPITTING OUT A PIECE OF GUM.<br />I TURNED TO SEE ONE MALE OFFICER PLACING THE GIRL IN CUFFS INTO THE BACK OF A SQUAD CAR WHILE TWO OTHER MALE OFFICERS STOOD BY THE OFFICER (I CAME LATER TO KNOW WAS OFFICER NELSON I WAS CONCERNED THAT THE GIRL&#39;S PARENTS SHOULD BE NOTIFIED). AND VERY SLOWLY SO AS NOT TO APPEAR A THREAT I APPROACHED THE OFFICERS TO FIND OUT THAT INFORMATION.  OFFICER NELSON WAS NOW IN THE FRONT SEAT ON THE RADIO.  I SAID EXCUSE ME OFFICER I AM A TEACHING ARTIST DIRECTING A PLAY HERE AT RAINIER BEACH AND WOULD LIKE TO KNOW WHAT THE GIRL IS BEING CHARGED AND AM CONCERNED ABOUT HER SAFETY.<br />I WAS ASKED WHAT MY RELATIONSHIP TO THE GIRL WAS.<br />I SAID SHE IS ONE OF MY STUDENTS&#39; CLASSMATES.<br />I WAS TOLD TO BACK UP BY OFFICER NELSON.<br />I DID BACK UP.<br />I ASKED AGAIN.<br />I WAS TOLD BY OFFICER ATOFAU TO BACK UP AS WELL.<br />I DID.<br />I ASKED AGAIN.<br />OFFICER NELSON GOT OUT OF HIS VEHICLE<br />GRABBED MY RIGHT ARM BEHIND MY BACK AND SLIGHTLY TWISTED IT AND HELD IT FOR SEVERAL SECONDS AS IF TO INSTIGATE SOME RESPONSE OR RESISTANCE.<br />WHEN I DID NOT RESIST<br />I WAS RELEASED AND TOLD TO PUT MY HANDS ON THE HOOD OF THE SQUAD CAR.<br />I THEN ASKED THE GIRL IN CUSTODY WHAT SHE WAS BEING CHARGED WITH.<br />SHE DID NOT RESPOND.<br />OFFICER NELSON ASKED ME MY NAME I GAVE IT.<br />AND TOLD HIM I HAVE NO RECORD AND REITERATED I AM A TEACHING ARTIST DIRECTING A PLAY HERE AT RAINIER BEACH.<br />OFFICER NELSON PROMPTED OFFICER ATOFAU TO CHECK ME FOR DRUGS AND WEAPONS.<br />MY POCKETS WERE EMPTIED AND MY BAG TAKEN<br />I WAS THEN TOLD BY OFFICER NELSON I WAS GOING TO JAIL TOO.<br />I ASKED FOR WHAT<br />AND WAS TOLD FOR INTERFERING.<br />I SAID THIS IS RIDICULOUS.<br />I JUST WANT TO MAKE SURE THE GIRL IS SAFE AND THAT HER PARENTS ARE NOTIFIED I HAVE NO RECORD AND I HAVE COMPLIED WITH YOUR REQUESTS.<br />I WAS PUT IN CUFFS AND TAKEN BY OFFICER ATOFAU TO THE OTHER<br />SQUAD CAR.<br />I YELLED TO TIA TO TELL BRANDIE FLOOD THE TRAINER ON TOBACCO THAT I HAD BEEN UNJUSTLY ARRESTED AND TO NOTIFY MY MOTHER.<br />I STILL HAD NOT BEEN READ MY RIGHTS OR GIVEN A CLEAR INDICATION OF WHAT MY OFFENSE HAD BEEN.<br />I WAS TAKEN TO THE SOUTH PRECINCT AND HELD IN CUSTODY FOR ABOUT 30MINUTES I BELIEVE<br />BEFORE MY RIGHTS WERE READ TO ME BY MY OFFICER ATOFAU.<br />SARGENT MCGINNIS AND OFFICER ATOFAU RETURNED TO GET<br />MY VERSION OF WHAT HAPPENED.<br />OFFICER NELSON AND OFFICER MCRAE CAME TO EXPRESSS NELSON VERSION OF WHAT HAD OCCURRED TO JUSTIFY MY ARREST.<br />I WAS TAKEN TO KING COUNTY APPROX 6:30PM STILL UNAWARE OF WHAT MY EXACT CHARGES WERE.<br />MY BELONGINGS WERE TRANSFERRED TO A PLASTIC BAG AND I WAS TOLD I WOULD HAVE TO RETRIEVE MY PUMA BAG FROM A SITE ON AIRPORT WAY.<br /> I WAS TOLD TO CHANGE INTO RED JAIL CLOTHING AND GIVEN A<br />SACK LUNCH AND PLACED IN A CELL.<br />FOR THE NEXT 5 1/2 HRS I WAS  TRANSFERRED FROM CELL TO CELL AND FINALLY RELEASED AT MIDNIGHT TO DISCOVER I HAD A HEARING FOR OBSTRUCTION OF A PUBLIC OFFICIAL.<br />THIS WAS THE FIRST TIME I WAS INFORMED OF WHAT I HAD BEEN ARRESTED FOR.<br />PLEASE ATTEND OR WRITE A LETTER OF REFERENCE<br />to rajniie@yahoo.com<br />Please call KOMO KIRO ALL MEDIA SOURCES<br />FLOOD THEM WITH THIS STORY<br /> - FOR QUESTIONS ON A CHILD&#39;S BEHALF<br /> A TEACHER MUST BE ARRESTED?!<br />MY HEARING IS ON APRIL 10TH @2:30PM 500 5TH AVE KING COUNTY CORRECTIONAL FACILITY.<br />PLEASE SUPPORT!<br />I GREATLY APPRECIATE IT!<br /> <br />PEACE,<br /> <br />RAJNII</div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-04-04 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>it&#39;s been too long since our last blog, folkers.<br /><br />first off, i&#39;d like to apologize for the lack of new mp3&#39;s available for your download at the upper right corner of this screen.  feel free to check out the new joint available that some of y&#39;all may be familiar with:  <a href="http://www.bluescholars.com/audio/Prometheus%20Brown%20-%20Kick%20Bush.mp3"><strong>Prometheus Brown - Kick Bush</strong></a><br />.  (&lt;--if the upper link ain&#39;t workin yet, just click on the link here) it&#39;s been performed at various smaller shows as well as making an appearance on a mixtape or two here and there.<br /><br />word on the block is that world famous <strong>DJ Topspin</strong> has dropped a new mixtape that is complete fire.  if any of you are familiar with Topspin <strong>(Tribal Music, Sinsemilla)</strong> then you know this man is a beast when it comes to mixtapes.  from <strong>Pillow Talk Volumes 1 to 7986</strong> to the <strong>Velour Vibes</strong> series to whatever, big tunes is his game.  i&#39;ve heard you can catch a copy of it at Earl&#39;s in the CD, or it should be available on his <strong><a href="http://www.topsyte.com/">website</a></strong> as well.<br /><br />i&#39;ll probably holla about this again later, but the homie Dan Dejos of <strong>Juxism</strong> hipped me to the grand opening of a spot catch all your favorite premium brands to stay fresh this spring.  where is it, you ask?  capitol hill?  soufcenner?  hell naw sun!  <strong>BELLINGHAM</strong>.  just another thing that shows the &#39;Ham culture is comin up in the world.  it ain&#39;t all just the Nightlight and Surge.  (haha, get at me cuzzo!)<br /><br /><img src="http://bp2.blogger.com/_6GCfUuzUAQE/RhGUss_pXRI/AAAAAAAAAAs/gv4ztcxqOXI/s1600/LOCUST_flyer_front%2B8.5X5.5_FINAL.jpg" alt="" /><img src="http://www.bluescholars.com/images/locust.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />peep the folks at <strong><a href="http://www.shoplocust.com/">Locust</a></strong> to snatch up the latest from GRNAPPLETREE and Orisue.  altho they&#39;re already receiving customers, they gotta grand opening event on April 28th, so at least be sure to give em a nod for puttin in mad work to bring more culture to the &#39;Ham.<br /><br />stay tuned, as we will be on this site talkin about more stuff.  interesting stuff.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-03-31 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://i12.tinypic.com/47vvabm.jpg" alt="" width="396" height="626" /><br /><br />Hey -- it had me laughing for hours when I saw it, and hey, I <em>made</em> it. <br /><br />Anyone trippin about the fact that Black Anger is finna rip the stage in May for the Blue Scholars Bayani release party?<br /><br />Is anyone finna check out the Dyme Def release party at the Vera Project tomorrow night? Click <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=1428.0" target="_blank">here</a> for more info, and check out me and Khingz as we open up the show. And no, don&#39;t expect any &quot;MC Rove&quot; references.<br /><br />Who <em>can&#39;t</em> get enough of the Native Guns &quot;Stray Bullets&quot; 2 CD?<br /><br />Who else is finna check out that &quot;Grindhouse&quot; double feature?<br /><br />Did anyone miss the Stop the Killings show last week? If you did, would you cop a STK mixtape? I need to holler at these amazing and talented <a href="http://wapifasa.org/wapifasa/" target="_blank">WAPIFASA</a> youth, mayne, so stay tuned.<br /><br />And If you&#39;re not paying attention, check out the calendar on the right for
latest Massline shows and artists to come to your town. Get home safe,
Gabe!<br /><br />Peace <br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> [38] <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="a